MindMirror — Complete Concept (Every Angle Covered)
💡 The Core Idea
An AI that acts as a cognitive personal trainer.

You bring it a problem, decision, or question. It never answers directly. Instead it:

Maps your thinking live
Exposes your blind spots and biases
Asks Socratic questions to push you deeper
Verifies any facts it references with transparent sourcing
Tracks your cognitive independence over time
Nudges you to think without AI when you've been over-relying on it
"The only AI built to make itself unnecessary."

🎯 The 3 Human Problems It Solves
Problem You Named	What's Happening	What MindMirror Does
Skill Degradation	People stop thinking because AI thinks for them	Forces a reasoning step before any AI engagement
Cognitive Surrender	People blindly accept AI output	AI shows why it flagged something + cites the psychological research behind it
Gradual Loss of Human Autonomy	Over time, humans stop trusting their own judgment	Tracks AI dependency score, nudges user to attempt problems alone, celebrates independent thinking
🧠 How the Experience Works
User: "Should I accept this job offer?"

Step 1 — Think First Gate
→ "Before we go further, what is your gut feeling and why?"
   User must type their own reasoning first.

Step 2 — Reasoning Map (Visual)
→ AI maps their reasoning as a live thought web
   Nodes: Assumptions | Emotions | Facts | Unknowns

Step 3 — Blind Spot Detection
→ "You assumed salary is the main factor — is that based on data or feeling?"
→ "You haven't considered long-term growth. Why?"
→ Each flag is tagged: [Confirmation Bias] [Availability Heuristic]
   with a citation: Kahneman, D. (2011). Thinking Fast and Slow.

Step 4 — Socratic Push
→ AI fires 2–3 sharp questions only — never gives the answer
→ "What would have to be true for this to be the wrong choice?"

Step 5 — Reflection + Clarity Score
→ User revisits their original answer — did it change?
→ Thinking Clarity Score shown (depth of reasoning, biases caught, unknowns identified)

Step 6 — 24hr Challenge (Learning Cycle)
→ "Come back tomorrow. Can you solve a similar problem without MindMirror?"
→ Spaced repetition loop — resurfaces problems you previously outsourced to AI

